{"record_id":"D36-B034","dataset_id":"D36","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Bug → Root Cause","subtopic":"Java Collection Mutation","concept":"Concurrent modification during iteration","knowledge_type":"FAILURE_MODE","question":"Why can modifying a Java collection during iteration cause ConcurrentModificationException or logically inconsistent traversal?","answer":"Many Java collection iterators detect structural modification after iterator creation and may fail fast with ConcurrentModificationException. Even when no exception occurs for a particular collection or operation, modifying the collection while traversal assumptions remain active can invalidate the intended iteration semantics.","explanation":"The diagnostic evidence is a structural collection mutation occurring outside the iterator's supported mutation mechanism. The root cause is violating the iterator/collection mutation contract.","principle":"Traversal and structural mutation must follow the collection's documented iterator contract.","objective":"Diagnose collection traversal failure caused by unsupported structural mutation.","requirements":["Structural modifications during iteration must use the supported mechanism or be deferred."],"constraints":["Exact behavior is collection and operation dependent."],"preconditions":["A collection is structurally modified while an iterator or enhanced-for traversal is active."],"input":"for (String value : values) { values.remove(value); }","output":"A fail-fast iterator may throw ConcurrentModificationException.","expected_behavior":"Use iterator-supported removal or collect changes and apply them after traversal.","incorrect_code":"for (String value : values) {\n    if (shouldRemove(value)) {\n        values.remove(value);\n    }\n}","corrected_code":"Iterator<String> iterator = values.iterator();\nwhile (iterator.hasNext()) {\n    String value = iterator.next();\n    if (shouldRemove(value)) {\n        iterator.remove();\n    }\n}","failure_mode":"Iterator invalidation or fail-fast exception.","expected_error":"ConcurrentModificationException may be thrown.","cause":"The collection is structurally modified outside the iterator's supported mutation protocol.","root_cause":"The code violates the collection traversal/mutation contract.","solution":"Use the iterator's supported removal operation, collection filtering APIs, or defer structural changes.","edge_case":"ConcurrentModificationException is not a synchronization primitive and its absence does not prove thread safety.","security_implication":"Incorrect collection mutation can cause incomplete filtering or authorization decisions when security-relevant entries are removed or processed.","performance_implication":"Repeated removal from certain collection types can have significant complexity costs; filtering strategy should match collection characteristics.","test_case":"Traverse collections containing removable and retained elements and verify the resulting collection.","test_input":"Mixed collection requiring multiple removals.","expected_test_result":"The corrected implementation removes intended elements without violating iterator semantics.","testing_guidance":"Test empty, single-element, all-remove, none-remove, and multiple-remove cases.","verification_method":"Iterator contract analysis plus collection behavior tests.","verification_guidance":"Distinguish fail-fast behavior from guaranteed thread-safety properties.","language":"Java","language_version":"Java 8+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Java 8+","dependencies":["Java Collections Framework"],"execution_requirements":["JVM"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"JAVA_COLLECTIONS_SEMANTICS","confidence":"HIGH","related_records":["D36-B015"],"depends_on":[],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":[],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"deri