{"record_id":"D36-B051","dataset_id":"D36","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Bug → Root Cause","subtopic":"Python Concurrency","concept":"Asyncio blocking call stalls the event loop","knowledge_type":"FAILURE_MODE","question":"Why can a blocking synchronous operation make unrelated Python asyncio tasks appear frozen?","answer":"A blocking synchronous operation executed directly inside an asyncio event-loop task prevents the event loop from running other scheduled tasks until the operation returns.","explanation":"Asyncio concurrency depends on cooperative execution. A task that performs blocking file, network, subprocess, or CPU work without yielding can occupy the event-loop thread and delay every other task sharing that loop.","principle":"Blocking operations must not monopolize the event-loop thread; use asynchronous APIs or explicitly offload blocking work.","objective":"Diagnose event-loop stalls caused by synchronous blocking operations in asynchronous Python code.","requirements":"The event loop must remain responsive to other scheduled tasks.","constraints":"Some operations are inherently synchronous and require explicit offloading rather than direct execution inside the event loop.","preconditions":"Multiple asyncio tasks share one event-loop thread.","input":"An async function containing a blocking synchronous operation.","output":"An asynchronous or explicitly offloaded implementation that allows the event loop to continue scheduling other tasks.","expected_behavior":"Other tasks continue making progress while the blocking operation is handled outside the event-loop thread.","incorrect_code":"async def fetch_data():\n    response = requests.get(url)\n    return response.text","corrected_code":"import asyncio\nimport requests\n\nasync def fetch_data():\n    response = await asyncio.to_thread(requests.get, url)\n    return response.text","failure_mode":"Event-loop starvation / blocking I/O","expected_error":"Usually no exception; latency increases and unrelated async tasks can stop making progress.","cause":"A synchronous blocking call executes on the event-loop thread.","root_cause":"The implementation violates the asynchronous execution model by performing blocking work without yielding or offloading it.","solution":"Use an async-native API or offload unavoidable blocking work with an appropriate executor/thread mechanism.","edge_case":"CPU-bound work can also block the event loop even when it is not I/O-bound and may require process-based parallelism rather than a thread.","security_implication":"Event-loop starvation can reduce responsiveness of security controls, request limits, timeouts, or authentication services and can contribute to resource exhaustion.","performance_implication":"One blocked event loop can amplify a single slow operation into high latency for many otherwise independent tasks.","test_case":"Schedule a periodic heartbeat alongside the blocking operation and verify that heartbeat execution remains within the accepted latency bound.","test_input":"A blocking request lasting several seconds while concurrent asyncio tasks are scheduled.","expected_test_result":"The event loop remains responsive and unrelated tasks continue according to their scheduling constraints.","testing_guidance":"Measure event-loop lag and run concurrency tests with deliberately slow blocking operations.","verification_method":"Inspect every synchronous call reachable from event-loop tasks and determine whether it can block for meaningful time.","verification_guidance":"Static async syntax does not prove non-blocking behavior; inspect called libraries and their execution model.","language":"Python","language_version":"Python 3.11+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.9+","dependencies":"Python asyncio; synchronous dependency in illustrative example","execution_requirements":"Python runtime with asyncio event loop","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUS