{"record_id":"D36-B052","dataset_id":"D36","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Bug → Root Cause","subtopic":"JavaScript Object State","concept":"Shallow copy preserves nested object aliasing","knowledge_type":"FAILURE_MODE","question":"Why can modifying a nested property of a copied JavaScript object unexpectedly modify the original object?","answer":"Object spread and Object.assign create shallow copies. Nested objects and arrays remain shared references, so mutating a nested value through the copy also affects the original.","explanation":"The top-level object is new, but referenced nested objects are not recursively cloned. Code that assumes deep independence can therefore introduce hidden state coupling.","principle":"Copy depth must match the required ownership and mutation semantics.","objective":"Diagnose unexpected state changes caused by shallow-copy aliasing.","requirements":"Independent nested state requires an explicit deep-copy strategy or immutable data design.","constraints":"Structured cloning, serialization, and custom cloning have different supported types and semantics.","preconditions":"An object contains nested mutable objects or arrays.","input":"A shallow copy followed by nested mutation.","output":"Independent state or an intentionally immutable update.","expected_behavior":"Mutating the copied structure does not unexpectedly mutate the original when independent ownership is required.","incorrect_code":"const original = { user: { name: \"A\" } };\nconst copy = { ...original };\ncopy.user.name = \"B\";","corrected_code":"const original = { user: { name: \"A\" } };\nconst copy = structuredClone(original);\ncopy.user.name = \"B\";","failure_mode":"Reference aliasing / unintended shared mutation","expected_error":"No required runtime error; incorrect shared state is the observable failure.","cause":"The nested object remains referenced by both top-level objects.","root_cause":"The implementation assumes a shallow copy provides recursive ownership separation.","solution":"Use structuredClone where its semantics fit, create explicit immutable updates, or implement domain-specific cloning for unsupported types.","edge_case":"structuredClone does not preserve every JavaScript object type's behavior and cannot clone some values such as functions.","security_implication":"Unexpected shared mutation can corrupt authorization, session, configuration, or tenant-isolated state.","performance_implication":"Deep copying can increase CPU and memory usage; copying should be applied deliberately to the required ownership boundary.","test_case":"Mutate nested objects and arrays through the copy and verify the original remains unchanged when independence is required.","test_input":"Nested objects, arrays, and supported structured-clone values.","expected_test_result":"The original object retains its original nested state.","testing_guidance":"Test both top-level and nested mutations and explicitly document intentional shared references.","verification_method":"Trace object references and determine whether nested values are shared after each copy operation.","verification_guidance":"Do not infer deep-copy semantics from syntax such as spread or Object.assign.","language":"JavaScript","language_version":"ECMAScript 2021+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"ECMAScript 2021+","dependencies":"ECMAScript structuredClone where supported","execution_requirements":"JavaScript runtime implementing structuredClone for the corrected example","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_LANGUAGE_SEMANTICS","confidence":0.99,"related_records":[],"depends_on":[],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":[],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":"ECMAScript object-reference semantics and structured cloning specification/documentation.","created_at":