{"record_id":"D36-B057","dataset_id":"D36","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Bug → Root Cause","subtopic":"Go HTTP Lifecycle","concept":"HTTP response body not closed after client request","knowledge_type":"FAILURE_MODE","question":"Why can repeatedly making Go HTTP requests without closing response bodies exhaust connections or degrade client behavior?","answer":"An HTTP response body represents a resource that must be consumed and closed according to the client's connection-management expectations. Failing to close it can prevent connection reuse and accumulate resources.","explanation":"The HTTP response body is part of the response lifecycle even when the caller does not need its contents. Client code should close the body after the response is obtained, and when connection reuse is desired, consuming the body appropriately can also matter.","principle":"Every owned HTTP response body must have an explicit lifecycle and closure path.","objective":"Diagnose HTTP client resource leaks caused by unclosed response bodies.","requirements":"Response bodies must be closed on all relevant paths after a client request.","constraints":"Exact connection reuse behavior depends on the HTTP transport and how much of the response body is consumed.","preconditions":"Go code performs repeated HTTP client requests.","input":"HTTP requests whose response bodies are ignored without closure.","output":"Response handling with deterministic body closure.","expected_behavior":"Resources remain bounded and eligible for connection reuse according to the HTTP transport's semantics.","incorrect_code":"resp, err := http.Get(url)\nif err != nil {\n    return err\n}\nreturn nil","corrected_code":"resp, err := http.Get(url)\nif err != nil {\n    return err\n}\ndefer resp.Body.Close()\nreturn nil","failure_mode":"HTTP resource leak / connection reuse degradation","expected_error":"Potential connection exhaustion, increased resource usage, or degraded networking behavior under repeated load.","cause":"The response body remains open after the request completes.","root_cause":"The response lifecycle is not explicitly closed by the owning code.","solution":"Close resp.Body on every successful response path, normally immediately after error checking.","edge_case":"If the caller needs to inspect the body asynchronously or transfer ownership, the ownership contract must explicitly identify who closes it.","security_implication":"Resource exhaustion from leaked responses can become a denial-of-service vector under repeated requests.","performance_implication":"Unclosed bodies can reduce connection reuse and increase connection establishment and resource consumption.","test_case":"Perform many requests against a controlled server and monitor open connections and resource usage.","test_input":"Repeated successful and failing HTTP responses under concurrency.","expected_test_result":"Response resources remain bounded and the client maintains expected connection behavior.","testing_guidance":"Use transport metrics, connection tracing, and leak detection under repeated load.","verification_method":"Trace ownership of every response body from acquisition to closure or explicit ownership transfer.","verification_guidance":"Check both success and error paths and review helper functions that may obscure response ownership.","language":"Go","language_version":"Go 1.20+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Go 1.13+","dependencies":"Go net/http","execution_requirements":"Go runtime and controlled HTTP test server","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_LIBRARY_SEMANTICS","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D36-B038"],"depends_on":[],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":[],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":"Go net/http package documentation and established HTTP resou