{"record_id":"D36-B058","dataset_id":"D36","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Bug → Root Cause","subtopic":"JavaScript Error Boundaries","concept":"Unhandled promise rejection escapes intended failure handling","knowledge_type":"FAILURE_MODE","question":"How can an asynchronous JavaScript operation fail outside a caller's intended error-handling path?","answer":"A promise rejection must be observed through await within an appropriate try/catch or through a rejection handler. If a promise is created and its rejection is neither awaited nor handled, the failure can escape the intended control flow.","explanation":"Synchronous try/catch only observes errors thrown during synchronous execution. A promise created inside the block may reject later, after the synchronous block has already completed, unless the promise is awaited or explicitly handled.","principle":"Asynchronous failure paths must be connected to the lifecycle and error boundary of the operation that owns them.","objective":"Diagnose unhandled promise rejections caused by detached asynchronous operations.","requirements":"Every owned promise must have a deliberate rejection-handling strategy.","constraints":"Fire-and-forget tasks can be valid, but they require an explicit policy for failures and lifecycle management.","preconditions":"An asynchronous function starts work that can reject independently of the caller's immediate synchronous execution.","input":"A promise started without awaiting or attaching a rejection handler.","output":"A handled or awaited promise whose failure reaches the intended error boundary.","expected_behavior":"Asynchronous failures are observed and handled according to the operation's contract.","incorrect_code":"function save() {\n    try {\n        writeAsync();\n    } catch (err) {\n        handleError(err);\n    }\n}","corrected_code":"async function save() {\n    try {\n        await writeAsync();\n    } catch (err) {\n        handleError(err);\n    }\n}","failure_mode":"Unhandled promise rejection / detached async failure","expected_error":"An unhandled rejection may be reported by the runtime and may leave the application state inconsistent depending on surrounding logic.","cause":"The promise is not awaited or given an explicit rejection handler.","root_cause":"The asynchronous operation is detached from the error boundary that was intended to govern it.","solution":"Await the operation when its completion belongs to the current lifecycle, or explicitly handle its rejection when it is intentionally detached.","edge_case":"A detached background task may require cancellation, logging, retry, and shutdown coordination in addition to rejection handling.","security_implication":"Suppressed asynchronous failures can leave security-sensitive state transitions incomplete while callers believe an operation succeeded.","performance_implication":"Repeated detached failures can create retries, resource leaks, or background work that continues after its initiating operation has ended.","test_case":"Force the asynchronous operation to reject and verify that the intended error handler executes.","test_input":"writeAsync() returning a rejected promise.","expected_test_result":"handleError receives the failure and the caller does not silently report success.","testing_guidance":"Test both synchronous throws and asynchronous rejections because they exercise different error paths.","verification_method":"Trace every created promise and identify where fulfillment and rejection are observed.","verification_guidance":"A surrounding synchronous try/catch is not sufficient evidence that asynchronous failures are handled.","language":"JavaScript","language_version":"ECMAScript 2022+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"ECMAScript 2017+","dependencies":"ECMAScript Promise and async/await","execution_requirements":"JavaScript runtime supporting Promises and async/await","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_sta