or sizes prevent efficient reuse of free memory.","optimization":"Reduce allocation churn, improve object lifetime locality, or use allocator-supported strategies where justified.","verification_method":"Compare live memory, resident memory, allocation histograms, fragmentation indicators, and latency over representative workloads.","performance_claim_type":"MEASURED_REQUIRED","validation_status":"METHODOLOGY_RULE","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","provenance_basis":["Runtime memory-management documentation","Allocator documentation"],"related_records":["D39-B016","D39-B045","D39-B239"],"relationships":["MEMORY_LIFETIME_DEPENDENT","REQUIRES_MEMORY_PROFILE"]} {"record_id":"D39-B241","dataset_id":"D39","dataset_version":"1.0","batch":"B49","knowledge_type":"PERFORMANCE_CASE","topic":"Cache Architecture","subtopic":"Multi-Level Cache Placement","objective":"Reduce latency and backend load by placing reusable data at an appropriate cache layer.","requirements":["Data consistency and invalidation requirements must be explicit","Each cache layer must have bounded resource policies"],"constraints":["Additional cache layers increase complexity","Stale data risk increases with longer retention"],"implementation_pattern":"Use local, shared, or edge cache layers according to data locality, consistency requirements, object size, and access frequency.","failure_mode":"A single cache layer is overloaded or remote access remains expensive despite repeated reads.","root_cause":"Cache placement does not match request locality or data-sharing requirements.","optimization":"Distribute caching across suitable layers while defining ownership, TTL, invalidation, and fallback behavior.","verification_method":"Measure cache hit rate by layer, latency, backend load, memory usage, and stale-data incidents.","performance_claim_type":"INFERRED","validation_status":"DOCUMENTED_PATTERN","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","provenance_basis":["Caching-system documentation","Distributed-systems caching literature"],"related_records":["D39-B011","D39-B012","D39-B013"],"relationships":["LAYERED_OPTIMIZATION","CONSISTENCY_TRADEOFF"]} {"record_id":"D39-B242","dataset_id":"D39","dataset_version":"1.0","batch":"B49","knowledge_type":"PERFORMANCE_CASE","topic":"Cache Management","subtopic":"Eviction Policy Selection","objective":"Improve cache effectiveness by selecting an eviction policy consistent with the workload's reuse pattern.","requirements":["Access pattern must be measurable","Cache implementation must support the chosen policy or equivalent"],"constraints":["No single eviction policy is optimal for all workloads","Policy metadata can increase memory or CPU overhead"],"implementation_pattern":"Evaluate workload locality and choose an eviction policy based on measured hit-rate and resource behavior rather than assuming a universal policy.","failure_mode":"Cache hit rate remains low despite sufficient nominal cache capacity.","root_cause":"Eviction policy discards objects with high future reuse or retains objects with little reuse.","optimization":"Select or tune eviction behavior using representative access traces.","verification_method":"Measure hit rate, eviction rate, memory overhead, latency, and backend request reduction.","performance_claim_type":"MEASURED_REQUIRED","validation_status":"METHODOLOGY_RULE","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","provenance_basis":["Caching-system documentation","Caching algorithm literature"],"related_records":["D39-B012","D39-B241","D39-B243"],"relationships":["WORKLOAD_DEPENDENT","CACHE_POLICY_REQUIRES_MEASUREMENT"]} {"record_id":"D39-B243","dataset_id":"D39","dataset_version":"1.0","batch":"B49","knowledge_type":"PERFORMANCE_CASE","topic":"Cache Management","subtopic":"Cache Admission","objective":"Prevent low-value objects from consuming cache capacity and displacing frequently reused data.","requirements":["The workload must provide enough evidence to estimate object reuse value","Admission logic must remain bounded in 