{"record_id":"D39-B301","dataset_id":"D39","dataset_version":"1.0","batch":"B61","topic":"Database Partition-Wise Join","knowledge_type":"PERFORMANCE_CASE","objective":"Reduce database join cost by aligning partitioning so corresponding partitions can be joined independently.","principle":"When compatible partition keys and predicates allow partition-wise execution, the database may avoid comparing unrelated partitions and reduce scanned data.","requirements":["Partitioning schemes must be compatible or transformable","Join predicates must preserve partition locality","The optimizer must support the applicable partition-wise strategy"],"constraints":["Partitioning can increase write and maintenance complexity","Skewed partitions can create stragglers","Optimizer behavior is database-version specific"],"failure_mode":"A join scans or compares substantially more partition data than necessary.","diagnosis":"Inspect the execution plan for partition pruning and partition-wise join behavior, then compare scanned partitions with the logical join scope.","optimization":"Align compatible partition keys and predicates where workload evidence shows that partition-wise execution materially reduces work.","verification_method":"Compare execution plans and measured resource consumption before and after the partitioning change using representative workloads.","performance_claim_type":"MEASURED_OR_UNKNOWN","validation_status":"STRUCTURAL","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","provenance":"Database optimizer and partitioning behavior must be validated against the target database documentation and version.","related_records":["D39-B201","D39-B256"],"relationships":[{"type":"EXTENDS","target":"D39-B201"},{"type":"RELATED_TO","target":"D39-B256"}]} {"record_id":"D39-B302","dataset_id":"D39","dataset_version":"1.0","batch":"B61","topic":"Database Join Order Optimization","knowledge_type":"OPTIMIZATION","objective":"Reduce intermediate result sizes and join work by selecting an execution or