faces, or unsafe development behavior.","root_cause":"Environment configuration does not explicitly disable development features in production.","remediation":"Define environment-specific configuration with production-safe debug settings and verify effective runtime state.","testing_method":"Deployment configuration test.","expected_test_result":"Production deployment reports debug/development features disabled.","verification_method":"Inspect effective runtime configuration and intentionally trigger a controlled error to verify production error behavior.","validation_status":"STRUCTURALLY_VALIDATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"VERIFIED_FACT","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":["OWASP ASVS","framework-specific official documentation where applicable"],"related_records":["D40-B081","D40-B085"],"relationships":{"extends":["D40-B081"],"verifies":["D40-B085"]}} {"record_id":"D40-B085","dataset_id":"D40","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B017","topic":"Security Problem → Remediation","subtopic":"Debug verification","concept":"Production debug-state verification","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","question":"How should production debug remediation be verified?","answer":"Verify the effective runtime environment identifies production mode and that diagnostic behavior exposed by development configuration is absent.","verification_method":"Configuration inspection plus controlled error-path testing in an authorized non-production environment that matches production settings.","validation_status":"STRUCTURALLY_VALIDATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"VERIFIED_FACT","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":["OWASP ASVS"],"related_records":["D40-B084"],"relationships":{"verifies":["D40-B084"]}} {"record_id":"D40-B086","dataset_id":"D40","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B018","topic":"Security Problem → Remediation","subtopic":"API security","concept":"Mass-assignment remediation","knowledge_type":"CODE_TRANSFORMATION","objective":"Prevent clients from modifying security-sensitive or server-controlled fields through generic object binding.","requirements":["Define writable fields explicitly","Reject or ignore protected fields","Validate authorization for permitted updates"],"failure_mode":"Generic request-to-object binding allows a caller to modify fields that should be controlled only by the server.","root_cause":"The input model exposes more writable properties than the business operation permits.","remediation":"Use an allowlisted input model or explicit field mapping for each update operation.","testing_method":"Negative API tests attempting to submit protected fields.","expected_test_result":"Protected fields remain unchanged and permitted fields update according to policy.","verification_method":"Inspect request model and persistence mapping and execute protected-field regression tests.","validation_status":"STRUCTURALLY_VALIDATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"VERIFIED_FACT","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":["OWASP API Security guidance","OWASP ASVS"],"related_records":["D40-B087","D40-B088"],"relationships":{"requires":["D40-B087"],"verifies":["D40-B088"]}} {"record_id":"D40-B087","dataset_id":"D40","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B018","topic":"Security Problem → Remediation","subtopic":"Input model design","concept":"Explicit writable-field model","knowledge_type":"PATTERN","objective":"Represent API update permissions through explicit input models rather than unrestricted entity binding.","explanation":"Separating external input models from persistence entities makes server-controlled properties explicit and reduces accidental privilege exposure.","security_implication":"An allowlist of writable fields reduces mass-assignment risk.","verification_method":"Compare request model fields with the documented mutation contract.","validation_status":"STRUCTURALLY_VALIDATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXEC